  3. Defending Network Endpoints.

  The GPL states that if you modify the Program and make the modified
Program available over a network (including the Internet) to others,
you must provide or offer to provide the Corresponding Source of the
modified Program to them.  This requirement applies both to
distributing copies of the covered work and to making modified
covered works available over a network.

  However, this requirement does not apply if you did not design the
Program for use over a network, and you make the modified Program
available only to a limited number of people through a file sharing
service or similar mechanism, as long as you take reasonable steps to
prevent users from downloading the covered work from your server if
you are not also distributing the covered work yourself.  This
provision is designed to prevent the common practice of "online
services" that take GPL code and make it available only through a web
interface, without offering downloads of the source code.

